  "landfallEstimate": "Movement towards Andhra Pradesh coast",
  "rawBulletin": "India Meteorological Department\n(Ministry of Earth Sciences)\nNATIONAL BULLETIN NO. 2 (BOB/10/2026)\nTIME OF ISSUE:1330 HOURS IST DATED:15.11.2026\nFROM: INDIA METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (FAX NO. 24643965/24699216/24623220)\nTO: CONTROL ROOM, NDM, MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (FAX.NO. 23093750)\nCONTROL ROOM NDMA (FAX.NO. 26701729)\nCABINET SECRETARIAT (FAX.NO.23012284, 23018638)\nPS TO HON\u2019BLE MINISTER FOR S & T AND EARTH SCIENCES (FAX NO.23316745)\nSECRETARY, MOES (FAX NO. 24629777)\nH.Q. (INTEGRATED DEFENCE STAFF AND CDS) (FAX NO. 23005137/23005147)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DOORDARSHAN (23385843)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, AIR (23421105, 23421219)\nPIB MOES (FAX NO. 23389042)\nUNI (FAX NO. 23355841)\nD.G. NATIONAL DISASTER RESPONSE FORCE (NDRF) (FAX NO. 26105912, 2436 3260)\nDIRECTOR, PUNCTUALITY, INDIAN RAILWAYS (FAX NO. 23388503)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDAMAN & NICOBAR ISLANDS (FAX NO. 03192-232656)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDHRA PRADESH (FAX NO. 0863-2441029)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ODISHA (FAX NO. 0674-2536660)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT OF TELANGANA (FAX NO 040-23455340)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TAMIL NADU (FAX NO. 044-25672304)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF PUDUCHERRY (FAX NO. 0413-2334145)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF CHHATTISGARH (FAX NO. 0771-2221206)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF JHARKHAND (FAX NO. 0651-2400255)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF WEST BENGAL (FAX NO. 033-22144328)\nSub: Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal [Pre Cyclone\nWatch for Andhra Pradesh & adjoining South Odisha coasts].\nThe Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal moved nearly northwards with the\nspeed of 10 kmph during past 03 hours and lay centered at 0830 hours IST of today, the 15th November,\n2026 over the same region, near Latitude 9.3\u00b0N and Longitude 86.9\u00b0E, about 630 km east of Trincomalee\n(Sri Lanka), 690km west-southwest of Sri Vijaya Puram (Andaman & Nicobar Islands), 840 km east-\nsoutheast of Chennai (Tamil Nadu), 1010 km south-southeast of Visakhapatnam (Andhra Pradesh) and\n1130 km south-southeast of Gopalpur (Odisha).\nIt is very likely to move north-northwestwards, intensify further into a Cyclonic Storm over the central parts\nof south & adjoining westcentral Bay of Bengal on 16th November and into a Severe Cyclonic Storm over\nwestcentral Bay of Bengal on 17th November, 2026. Thereafter, it is likely to intensify further and move\nnorthwestwards towards Andhra Pradesh coast during subsequent 2 days.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(IST) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n15.11.26/0830 9.3/86.9 40-50 gusting to 60 Depression\n15.11.26/1730 10.0/86.8 50-60 gusting to 70 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/0530 10.6/86.7 55-65 gusting to 75 Deep Depression\n16.11.26/1730 11.3/86.5 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/0530 12.0 /86.3 75-85 gusting to 95 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1730 12.7/86.1 95-105 gusting to 115 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/0530 13.6/85.8 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/1730 14.6/85.4 110-120 gusting to 130 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/0530 15.7/85.0 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\nWarnings:\n(i) Rainfall Warning:\nAndaman & Nicobar Islands: Light to moderate rainfall at most places is very likely during 15th to 17th\nNovember.\nTamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at\nisolated places is very likely on 17th & 20th with heavy to very heavy rainfall at isolated places on 18th &\n19th November.\nCoastal Andhra Pradesh: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at isolated places\nis very likely on 18th, light to moderate rainfall at most places with heavy to very heavy rainfall at a few\nplaces over coastal Andhra Pradesh and with isolated extremely heavy rainfall (\u226521 cm) over north\ncoastal Andhra Pradesh on 19th & 20th November.\nOdisha: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at isol",
